B.akv=s(["Breadboard 5V and GND rails directly bridged together.","USB cable is charge-only without data wires.","Inductive motor drawing more than the 500mA USB current limit."],t.s)
B.XD=s(["Unplug the USB cable immediately.","Trace the power rail: verify no bare wires bridge the (+) and (-) rails.","Disconnect all motors or servos and power them with separate batteries.","Let the board cool down for 60 seconds.","Plug USB in: verify the green ON LED is bright and solid."],t.s)
B.OV=new A.jt("Power Failures & Short Circuit Protection",B.f5,"Arduino green ON LED is dark, board turns off immediately, or chip gets hot.","Ohm\u2019s law states I = V / R. When 5V connects directly to GND, resistance R is near zero, causing current I to surge toward infinity. The Arduino polyfuse cuts power to protect your computer motherboard.","Never let Red (+) and Blue/Black (-) touch without a component in between!",B.XD)
B.akr=s(["LED inserted backwards (anode and cathode flipped).","Active buzzer signal and ground pins swapped.","Electrolytic capacitor connected backwards (can burst if reverse-biased)."],t.s)
B.UD=s(["Inspect the component legs before inserting into breadboard.","Long leg (Anode) goes to the digital pin through a resistor.","Short leg (Cathode) with flat rim on plastic body goes to GND.","Always use a 220\u03a9 resistor with LEDs to prevent burning the silicon."],t.s)
B.OW=new A.jt("Reversed LEDs & Polarized Components",B.ef,"LED won\u2019t light, buzzer won\u2019t beep, or electrolytic capacitor gets warm.","Diodes and transistors are semiconductors made of P-type and N-type silicon. Current can only flow when the P-side is connected to positive and N-side to negative (forward bias). Reverse bias blocks all current.","Long Leg = Positive (+), Short Leg / Flat Edge = Negative (-).",B.UD)
B.aks=s(["Circuit has a 5V path but no return wire back to Arduino GND.","Using external battery for motors without connecting battery (-) to Arduino GND.","Broken jumper wire with internal snapped copper."],t.s)
B.V_=s(["Check that the breadboard blue/black rail has a jumper wire going to an Arduino GND pin.","If using an external battery, connect its (-) negative terminal to Arduino GND.","Verify digital pins have a pull-up or pull-down to prevent floating antenna noise."],t.s)
B.OT=new A.jt("Missing Grounds & Floating Circuit Loops",B.ef,"Circuits behave randomly, LEDs glow faintly, or readings jump wildly.","Electricity cannot flow without a continuous closed loop. Current leaves 5V, passes through the components doing work, and must return to GND. If GND is missing, electrons have nowhere to go.","All grounds must be shared! Every circuit needs a return path home.",B.V_)
B.akw=s(["Code defines pin 7 but wire is in pin 8.","Using analogWrite() on a non-PWM pin (missing tilde ~ mark).","Using attachInterrupt() on a pin other than 2 or 3 on Arduino Uno."],t.s)
B.VR=s(["Trace the jumper wire with your finger from breadboard to Arduino pin.","Double-check the pin declaration at the very top of your Arduino sketch.","For brightness/speed fading, verify the pin is marked with ~."],t.s)
B.OU=new A.jt("Pin Mismatches & Hardware Limitations",B.ef,"Code runs without errors, but the connected component never reacts.","Microcontroller pins have specialized hardware peripherals inside the silicon: timers for PWM (pins 3, 5, 6, 9, 10, 11), ADCs for analog input (pins A0-A5), and hardware interrupt lines (INT0 on pin 2, INT1 on pin 3).","Look for the squiggly tilde ~ for PWM fading, and check pin numbers twice!",B.VR)
B.akt=s(["Missing semicolon at the end of the previous line.","Typo in variable name or keyword (C++ is case sensitive).","Unbalanced curly braces { } causing function nesting errors."],t.s)
B.Wd=s(["Press Ctrl+T (Cmd+T on Mac) in the Arduino IDE to auto-indent your sketch.","Look at the very FIRST orange error message\u2014fixing it usually resolves subsequent errors.",'If it says "expected ;", check the line DIRECTLY ABOVE the red highlight.',"Ensure library headers like #include <Wire.h> are at the very top of the file."],t.s)
B.OS=new A.jt("Deciphering Arduino IDE Compiler Errors",B.jn,"Clicking Verify (check mark) turns the bottom console orange with error text.","The C++ compiler operates in passes: preprocessing, lexical tokenizing, syntax parsing, and code generation. When grammar rules are violated, the compiler cannot produce machine instructions.","Press Ctrl+T to Auto-Format! It instantly reveals missing braces and typos.",B.Wd)
B.aku=s(["Wires connected to Digital Pins 0 (RX) and 1 (TX) during sketch upload.","Wrong COM port or wrong Board model selected in Tools menu.","CH340 USB driver missing on computer."],t.s)
B.V6=s(["Temporarily pull out any wires connected to Pin 0 (RX) and Pin 1 (TX).",'Verify Tools -> Board is set to "Arduino Uno".',"Verify Tools -> Port has a checkmark next to your connected COM port.",'Click Upload. When "Done uploading" appears, re-insert wires into pins 0 and 1.'],t.s)
B.OR=new A.jt("Upload Timeouts & Serial Port Conflicts",B.hz,'Upload fails with "avrdude: stk500_recv(): programmer is not responding".',"The ATmega328P communicates with your PC via universal asynchronous receiver-transmitter (UART) lines routed to pins 0 and 1. If external devices pull those lines HIGH or LOW, the upload data packet frame is corrupted.","Unplug pins 0 and 1 before uploading! Plug them back in when done uploading.",B.V6)
B.UX=s([B.OV,B.OW,B.OT,B.OU,B.OS,B.OR],A.aq("u<jt>"))
